<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Washington returns two weeks after intake and is seen by Dr. Okoro-Lindqvist of prosthodontics on the same day. He has kept the lower denture out except at meals and the soreness has gone. He has used acetaminophen two or three times a week, most recently four days ago. He is eating soft food with protein at each meal and takes the oral supplement twice a day; his weight is 92.8 kg, up 0.4 kg. He rates his chewing 4 out of 10. Without the lower denture between meals he has avoided public speaking for a week, and with it the denture still lifts when he speaks. His upper and lower dentures are more than eight years old. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ulcers</td><td>No soreness for a week with the lower denture out between meals</td></tr><tr><td>Acetaminophen</td><td>Two or three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>92.8 kg, up 0.4 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Chewing</td><td>4 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Speech</td><td>Lower denture still lifts when he speaks</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

